    "https://www.lynn.edu/employment": {
      "title": "Employment",
      "description": "Employment | Lynn University Skip directly to page content Disable autoplay of videos Enable autoplay of videos Lynn University Search Menu Home Employment Employment Working at Lynn isn't just a job ... it's a mission. Our people are talented enough to do anything, but they choose to work at Lynn because they believe that they are contributing to something important. Our top priority is to support our students as they achieve their dreams—and we pride ourselves on finding intellectually fearless people who enable us to constantly improve and adapt. We embrace new ideas, and we continually challenge ourselves to be better, faster, first. Here, you’ll be free to think differently. We celebrate innovation and we don’t let bureaucracy get in the way of a good idea. Most importantly, Lynn employees go above and beyond for our students, parents, alumni and supporters. We’re available and responsive, and we learn from them just as much as they learn from us. Jobs at Lynn Employees at Lynn are members of a diverse workforce that help educate students from all over the world. Take a moment to explore part-time, full-time and student jobs for departments ranging from athletics to admission. External candidates Want to work at Lynn? Use our online portal and find your dream job. Current employees Employees can log into Workday to review applications and open positions. Current students Students can log into Workday and apply for open positions. Past students (after May 2020) Use a Workday login or contact eservices@lynn.edu if you're a first-time user. Benefits and wellness At Lynn, we provide comprehensive benefits from medical and educational plans to disability protection and legal services. We also offer ample paid holidays, sick leave and vacation time. As an employee, you'll have access to a variety of benefits, and you can choose which ones best suit you and your family. Employee benefits Plus, we equip employees with information on staying well, and host events dedicated to holistic health and fitness. Wellness programs Lynn people June 2026 Employee of the Month: Jeff Rozier Lynn University named Jeff Rozier, mover supervisor in Campus Operations, as June's Employee of the Month for his dedication. Read more News Burnstine examines the evolution of malls and retail stores Robert Watson presents America 250th anniversary lecture series at 92NY Lynn employees research explores education for sustainable development Tiffany Shierling and Kelly Burlison publish higher education article Read all news Contact us Online Employee Services Phone +1 561-237-7290 Email eservices@lynn.edu Office hours Monday–Friday, 9 a.m.–5 p.m. 1-800-994-LYNN Contact us Map & directions About Academics Admission & aid Student life Giving Connect with us: Facebook Connect with us: Twitter Connect with us: Instagram Connect with us: YouTube Connect with us: LinkedIn Accreditation Employment Accessibility University policies and bylaws Terms of use Privacy statement Consumer disclosures Ethics hotline EASE grant performance measures Copyright © 2026 Lynn University. All rights reserved. Search Go Popular topics Degree programs (majors & minors) Tuition, scholarships and financial aid Academic calendar Jobs, employment opportunities Transcript request About menu button trigger About Mission & strategy Location Lynn history Lynn facts Awards Leadership Employment Lynn traditions Academics menu button trigger Academics Areas of study Individualized learning Colleges Academic calendar Academic catalog Prior academic credits Core curriculum Admission menu button trigger Admission Apply to Lynn Visit Lynn Tuition & aid Student life menu button trigger Student life Campus safety Dining Health & wellness Housing Transportation Clubs & organizations Giving menu button trigger Giving Support arts & culture Support athletics Support academics Support campus Annual giving Ways to give Athletics Campus directory Campus store Career and Alumni Connections Events Library Map & directions OneCampus News Alumni Education counselors & consultants Employees Students Parents and families Partners and community"
